{"resource":{"id":"react-answer-key","title":"React.js — Answer Key","category":"Web Development","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"25 min","pages":34,"lastUpdated":"February 2026","tags":["Web Development","React","Hooks"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Complete answer key for React.js practice questions — detailed explanations, alternative approaches, optimization tips, performance notes, best practices, and evaluation rubrics."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"mcq","label":"MCQ Answers"},{"id":"debug","label":"Debug Walkthroughs"},{"id":"coding","label":"Coding Solutions"},{"id":"alternates","label":"Alternative Approaches"},{"id":"optimize","label":"Optimization Tips"},{"id":"perf","label":"Performance Notes"},{"id":"best","label":"Best Practices"},{"id":"rubric","label":"Evaluation Rubrics"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQs"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"React.js — Practice Questions","tag":"Web Development","time":"32 min"},{"title":"React.js — Interview Questions","tag":"Web Development","time":"34 min"},{"title":"React.js — Complete Tutorial","tag":"Web Development","time":"44 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Check answers with full explanations and edge cases.</li>\n          <li>See alternative implementations and trade-offs.</li>\n          <li>Grade your own work with published rubrics.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"/><path d=\"M9 18h6\"/><path d=\"M10 22h4\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Study method</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Attempt the question first, compare with the solution, then rewrite from memory.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"mcq\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">MCQ Answers</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>useFetch</strong> — not a built-in hook (it's a common custom hook).</li>\n          <li><strong>One root element</strong> — or a fragment.</li>\n          <li><strong>Stable unique id</strong> — prevents reconciliation bugs.</li>\n          <li><strong>Once on mount</strong> — empty deps run only after first render.</li>\n        </ol>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Grading flow: correctness → readability → performance → tests.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"debug\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Debug Walkthroughs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><strong>The broken counter:</strong> plain variable <code>let n = 0</code> is not React state, so incrementing doesn't trigger a re-render. Fix:</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>function C() {\n  const [n, setN] = useState(0);\n  return &lt;button onClick={() =&gt; setN(n + 1)}&gt;{n}&lt;/button&gt;;\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"coding\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Coding Solutions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><strong>Stopwatch:</strong></p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>function Stopwatch() {\n  const [ms, setMs] = useState(0);\n  const [running, setRunning] = useState(false);\n  useEffect(() =&gt; {\n    if (!running) return;\n    const id = setInterval(() =&gt; setMs(m =&gt; m + 10), 10);\n    return () =&gt; clearInterval(id);\n  }, [running]);\n  return (\n    &lt;div&gt;\n      &lt;div&gt;{(ms / 1000).toFixed(2)}s&lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;button onClick={() =&gt; setRunning(r =&gt; !r)}&gt;{running ? &quot;Pause&quot; : &quot;Start&quot;}&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button onClick={() =&gt; { setMs(0); setRunning(false); }}&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  );\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"alternates\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Alternative Approaches</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>The stopwatch above can also be implemented with <code>useReducer</code> for cleaner state transitions, or with <code>requestAnimationFrame</code> for smoother visual updates.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"optimize\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Optimization Tips</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Batch related state into a reducer.</li>\n          <li>Memoize handlers passed to memoized children.</li>\n          <li>Debounce/throttle high-frequency events.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"perf\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Performance Notes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Profile before optimizing. Premature memoization adds noise without a measured win.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555066931-4365d14bab8c?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Rubric: correctness (40%), readability (25%), performance (20%), tests (15%).\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"best\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Best Practices</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Descriptive component and hook names.</li>\n          <li>Small pure functions over large impure ones.</li>\n          <li>Type props with TypeScript.</li>\n          <li>Test the behavior, not the implementation.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"rubric\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Evaluation Rubrics</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Criterion</th><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Weight</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Correctness</td><td class=\"border p-2\">40%</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Readability</td><td class=\"border p-2\">25%</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Performance</td><td class=\"border p-2\">20%</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Tests</td><td class=\"border p-2\">15%</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Answers are a starting point. Rewrite each solution in your own style and add tests.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Are these the only correct answers?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No — many approaches are valid. The rubric measures quality, not conformity.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Further Reading &amp; References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Answer key — verify solutions against the current React version.</p>\n      </div></section>"}